# Observability Console (FEATURE-DEV-CONSOLE-OBSERVABILITY-1)

Authority: `docs/architecture/observability-console.md`. Extends ENT-7 (developer
console) and OBS-1 (request id); replaces neither.

1. **Never log raw passwords, tokens, cookies, KTP/NIK, clinical notes, SOAP, raw RME
   payload, odontogram payload, or sensitive request bodies into observability
   telemetry.** Request bodies, query strings and SQL bindings are never read.
2. **New modules/routes must remain compatible with request correlation and
   observability instrumentation unless explicitly excluded** — add an exclusion only
   in `config/observability_console.php` `exclude`, with a reason (health probes,
   polling).
3. **Observability must remain bounded-retention and must not materially degrade
   production request performance.** Writes happen only in `terminate()` (after the
   response is sent); every console read is windowed, limited or paginated; no new
   daemon; retention is the per-request lottery plus `observability:prune`.
4. All text reaching `sys_obs_*` passes `TelemetryRedactor` (route templates, redacted
   messages, argument-free relative traces, normalized SQL). Never copy its rules.
5. Telemetry never throws, never `report()`s from inside a request, and writes only to
   `sys_obs_*`. Never call `BranchContext::forUser()` from telemetry — it can write.
6. Console routes stay `developer-console.*`, GET-only, `permission:view_developer_console`
   (Super Admin only), audited via `DeveloperConsoleService::recordAccess`.
   `developer-console.index` keeps its name (ENT-7 governance looks it up).
7. Thresholds live only in `config/observability_console.php`.
8. Say the scope: app cache hit rate ≠ Redis **server** hit rate; branch beside an event
   is an observation, not authority; the app sees PHP timeouts only — never claim to
   detect nginx 499/502/504 or client RTO.
9. Redis is probed only when used as cache/session/queue backend; otherwise
   `NOT_IN_USE`. Surface only allow-listed INFO counters; on failure report the
   exception class, never its message.
10. Tests: phpunit.xml sets `OBSERVABILITY_TELEMETRY_ENABLED=false`; observability
    suites enable it explicitly. Never re-enable it suite-wide — query-budget tests
    would measure telemetry instead of the app.
